{"crc":"06a10b8c","kind":"Candidate","payload":{"response":"Looking at the issue, the problem is that `AlterOrderWithRespectTo` needs to be generated before `AddIndex` operations that reference the `_order` field. The `_order` field is created by `AlterOrderWithRespectTo`, so any index that references it must come after.\n\nThe fix should be in the `_detect_changes` method in `django/db/migrations/autodetector.py`. Currently, `generate_altered_order_with_respect_to()` is called after `generate_added_indexes()`. We need to move it before the index generation operations.\n\nHere's the fix:\n\n# path: django/db/migrations/autodetector.py\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n        # Generate index removal operations before field is removed\n        self.generate_removed_constraints()\n        self.generate_removed_indexes()\n        # Generate field operations\n        self.generate_renamed_fields()\n        self.generate_removed_fields()\n        self.generate_added_fields()\n        self.generate_altered_fields()\n        self.generate_altered_unique_together()\n        self.generate_altered_index_together()\n        self.generate_added_indexes()\n        self.generate_added_constraints()\n        self.generate_altered_db_table()\n        self.generate_altered_order_with_respect_to()\n=======\n        # Generate index removal operations before field is removed\n        self.generate_removed_constraints()\n        self.generate_removed_indexes()\n        # Generate field operations\n        self.generate_renamed_fields()\n        self.generate_removed_fields()\n        self.generate_added_fields()\n        self.generate_altered_fields()\n        self.generate_altered_unique_together()\n        self.generate_altered_index_together()\n        self.generate_altered_order_with_respect_to()\n        self.generate_added_indexes()\n        self.generate_added_constraints()\n        self.generate_altered_db_table()\n>>>>>>> REPLACE","round":1,"slot":0},"producer":{"instance":"01KZQAN0VZE5SZHRRA9V5AE4B1","kind":"drafter","parent":"01KZQAN0VSS7PT1BB0NW5RY1ZT"},"schema":"Candidate@1","seq":14,"t":1786415582.206441}
{"crc":"14e8ce11","kind":"substrate.TriggerFired","payload":{"factory":"validator","firing_key":null,"input_sha256":"sha256:62d0eaa55793d20f2852896fbe4743f6606f8dc8e76fb2a7e461b9a6908d1e40","instance":"01KZQAN2ZY58V43P0E7WBDYPR8","resolved_input":{"response":"Looking at the issue, the problem is that `AlterOrderWithRespectTo` needs to be generated before `AddIndex` operations that reference the `_order` field. The `_order` field is created by `AlterOrderWithRespectTo`, so any index that references it must come after.\n\nThe fix should be in the `_detect_changes` method in `django/db/migrations/autodetector.py`. Currently, `generate_altered_order_with_respect_to()` is called after `generate_added_indexes()`. We need to move it before the index generation operations.\n\nHere's the fix:\n\n# path: django/db/migrations/autodetector.py\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n        # Generate index removal operations before field is removed\n        self.generate_removed_constraints()\n        self.generate_removed_indexes()\n        # Generate field operations\n        self.generate_renamed_fields()\n        self.generate_removed_fields()\n        self.generate_added_fields()\n        self.generate_altered_fields()\n        self.generate_altered_unique_together()\n        self.generate_altered_index_together()\n        self.generate_added_indexes()\n        self.generate_added_constraints()\n        self.generate_altered_db_table()\n        self.generate_altered_order_with_respect_to()\n=======\n        # Generate index removal operations before field is removed\n        self.generate_removed_constraints()\n        self.generate_removed_indexes()\n        # Generate field operations\n        self.generate_renamed_fields()\n        self.generate_removed_fields()\n        self.generate_added_fields()\n        self.generate_altered_fields()\n        self.generate_altered_unique_together()\n        self.generate_altered_index_together()\n        self.generate_altered_order_with_respect_to()\n        self.generate_added_indexes()\n        self.generate_added_constraints()\n        self.generate_altered_db_table()\n>>>>>>> REPLACE","round":1,"slot":0},"trigger_id":"validate"},"producer":null,"schema":"substrate.TriggerFired@1","seq":15,"t":1786415582.206629}
